# Backend API Conventions

Layering: `routes/` (thin) → `controllers/` (parse + shape response) →
`services/` (business logic) → Prisma → MySQL. See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Data access — Prisma is the standard

- Use Prisma (`@prisma/client`) for ALL DB operations. Do NOT add new `mysql2`
  pool queries (`pool.execute` / `pool.query`).
- A legacy raw-pool layer still exists (`config/database.ts` + some
  `repositories/`). It is being migrated onto Prisma. When you touch one of
  those files, prefer converting it rather than adding more raw SQL.
- Admin CRUD controllers are all on Prisma + the `AppError` envelope now —
  `insightsAdminKpi`, `insightsAdminPage`, `insightsAdminSourceReport`
  (uses the `IeSourceReport` model), and `insightsAdminIngestion`. Mirror them.
- Do NOT "convert" the Insights **data-warehouse** layer (`services/QC*Data.ts`,
  `QCKpiService`, `workers/`, rollups, `insightsQC`/`insights` read controllers):
  it is deliberately hand-written SQL for analytical performance — see
  [.cursor/rules/insights-data-warehouse.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/insights-data-warehouse.mdc).

## Error / response envelope (review items #23, #89)

There is a canonical policy in [backend/src/utils/errorHandler.ts](mdc:backend/src/utils/errorHandler.ts). Only three shapes are allowed:

- (A) Rich envelope — throw `AppError` (or `createValidationError` /
  `createNotFoundError` / etc.) and let the global `errorHandler` render it.
  Wrap async handlers in `asyncHandler`. Use this for ALL new controller errors.
- (B) Flat auth envelope — `ApiErrors.*` from `utils/apiError.ts`, only in
  auth/authorization middleware that short-circuits before a controller.
- (C) Legacy `{ success, message, data }` — do NOT add to new handlers. Existing
  (C) call sites migrate to (A) endpoint-by-endpoint.

Do not invent a fourth shape. Throw, don't hand-roll `res.status().json({ error })`.

## Validation & logging

- Validate all request input with Zod schemas in `validation/`.
- Log with Winston (`config/logger.ts`); never `console.log` in request paths.

## Size & duplication

- Refactor controllers/services at 200–300 lines; keep business logic in services.
- Before adding a helper (pagination parsing, date formatting, response shaping),
  search for an existing one — these are frequently duplicated.
